    "overviewMarkdown": "# Salivo Language Tools\n\nOfficial Salivo Language Support for modern high-performance systems programming.\n\n### What is Salivo?\nSalivo is a compiled programming language built around native stream header imports (`><`), deterministic RAII memory management via the `pub trait Drop` protocol, zero-underscore type law, and ultra-fast compilation via the `sf` CLI toolchain.\n\n### Core Language Features\n- **Stream Header Imports (`><`):** Visual stream flow representing input modules flowing directly into compilation units (`>< \"lib/math.sal\"`).\n- **Strict Static Type Safety:** `int`, `float`, `bool`, `string`, `Option<T>`, `Result<T, E>`, `Vec<T>`, `Map<K, V>`.\n- **Deterministic RAII Drop:** Automatic zero-overhead resource destruction upon scope termination.\n- **Error Handling (`?`):** Idiomatic error propagation with the `?` operator on `Result<T, E>`.\n- **Integrated sf Toolchain:** Immediate compilation and direct binary execution in the built-in terminal via `sf run <file>`."
